# GO-2026-5932: govulndb flags golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp as unmaintained
# and unsafe by design. The server never imports that subpackage — x/crypto
# is only pulled in for bcrypt/ssh/chacha20 (`go mod why -m golang.org/x/crypto`
# -> internal/auth -> bcrypt; `go list -deps ./...` has no openpgp entry).
# The advisory carries no CVSS score (severity UNKNOWN, tag "note") and no
# fixed version — govulncheck, which does reachability analysis, already
# passes clean on this repo. Trivy's Go-binary scanner flags the whole
# x/crypto module regardless of which subpackages actually got linked in,
# which is why this alone was intermittently failing the blocking
# CRITICAL/HIGH gate with no code change involved.
GO-2026-5932
